---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LegalPage from "../../components/LegalPage.astro";
import {
  CONTACT_EMAIL,
  FREESTYLE_ACCOUNT_DELETION_MAILTO,
  LEGAL_FREESTYLE_LAST_UPDATED,
  THIRD_PARTY_POLICY_URLS,
} from "../../constants";
---

<BaseLayout title="Account Deletion | Freestyle Rap" canonicalPath="/freestyle-rap/delete-account">
  <LegalPage eyebrow="Freestyle Rap" themeColor="app-freestyle">
    <h1>Freestyle Rap account deletion request</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {LEGAL_FREESTYLE_LAST_UPDATED}</p>

    <p>
      This page explains how to request deletion of your Freestyle Rap account and associated cloud data. Freestyle Rap
      is provided by Lyricspiration and Khonsu Development (the &quot;Service Provider&quot;).
    </p>

    <h2>How to request account deletion</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Open Freestyle Rap on your device and note the <strong>Google account email</strong> shown in account settings
        (or the email you used to sign in with Google).
      </li>
      <li>
        Send an email to <a href={FREESTYLE_ACCOUNT_DELETION_MAILTO}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> from that same Google account
        address. Use the subject line &quot;Freestyle Rap account deletion request&quot; and include the Google account
        email in the message body.
      </li>
      <li>
        The Service Provider verifies that you own the account, then deletes your Firebase account and linked cloud
        data described below.
      </li>
      <li>The Service Provider confirms by email when deletion is complete.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      <a href={FREESTYLE_ACCOUNT_DELETION_MAILTO}>Request account deletion by email</a>
    </p>

    <h2>What will be deleted</h2>
    <p>When your request is processed, the Service Provider deletes cloud data tied to your Google-linked account:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Your Firebase Authentication profile linked to Google (for example, your email address and profile photo
        reference).
      </li>
      <li>Synced favorite beats stored in Firebase.</li>
      <li>
        Cloud purchase entitlements and related verification metadata stored in Firebase (for example, unlocked beat
        product IDs and purchase tokens used to enforce entitlements).
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What is not deleted</h2>
    <p>The following data is not removed by an account deletion request, or is not controlled by the Service Provider:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Local app data on your device</strong>, including freestyle recordings, app settings, cached beat files,
        and offline purchase state. Delete recordings in the app or uninstall Freestyle Rap to remove local data.
      </li>
      <li>
        Data held by <a href={THIRD_PARTY_POLICY_URLS.googlePlayTerms}>Google Play</a> (billing and purchase history),
        <a href={THIRD_PARTY_POLICY_URLS.firebasePrivacy}>Firebase Analytics</a> and Crashlytics, and{" "}
        <a href={THIRD_PARTY_POLICY_URLS.googleAdMob}>Google AdMob</a>, retained according to their policies.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Purchase refunds</strong>: deleting your account does not refund past purchases. If you sign in again
        later with the same Google account, Google Play purchases may be restored when the app re-verifies them.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Processing time</h2>
    <p>
      Verified account deletion requests are processed within <strong>30 days</strong>. The Service Provider may contact
      you if additional verification is needed.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about account deletion, contact the Service Provider at{" "}
      <a href={FREESTYLE_ACCOUNT_DELETION_MAILTO}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</BaseLayout>
